{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794559549719,"sessionID":"ses_e2bee348affe4Stcilr5Lp7I7h","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4159d17001z7HJ9cKXTNYB5S","sessionID":"ses_e2bee348affe4Stcilr5Lp7I7h","messageID":"msg_1d41575c5001Sgh07RVFFqS3UZ","type":"tool","id":"call_a358b5ba397e41bfb8163b8f","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" --glob '!specs/**' --glob '!node_modules/**' . | head -20; echo \"exit=$?\"","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:50:The deriver also updates generated projection blocks in the live TypeScript and Python scoring sources. Its `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `lib/command-attach.ts` holds `COMMAND_ROWS`, one row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry, covering the entry id and every enabled runtime id. Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill. The same block holds `COMMAND_POLICIES`, one policy per runnable string, so a surface that attaches a command can name its policy without a second lookup. It writes the `MODE_COMMANDS` block into the same file, one row per hub mode that names a command, and fails when a mode names a command with no file under `.skilled/commands/`. The same block also holds `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, one row per tracked command keyed by its runnable string, emitted for every bridge entry whether or not the bridge is active. Each TypeScript bridge in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` carries an `ownerSkill`, the skill that owns its command. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:86:    expect('COMMAND_POLICIES' in await import('../lib/command-attach.js')).toBe(false);\nexit=0\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/README.md:50:The deriver also updates generated projection blocks in the live TypeScript and Python scoring sources. Its `GENERATED COMMAND ROWS` block in `lib/command-attach.ts` holds `COMMAND_ROWS`, one row per id a scorer can return for an enabled entry, covering the entry id and every enabled runtime id. Each row carries the runnable slash command, its derived policy and the owning skill. The same block holds `COMMAND_POLICIES`, one policy per runnable string, so a surface that attaches a command can name its policy without a second lookup. It writes the `MODE_COMMANDS` block into the same file, one row per hub mode that names a command, and fails when a mode names a command with no file under `.skilled/commands/`. The same block also holds `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, one row per tracked command keyed by its runnable string, emitted for every bridge entry whether or not the bridge is active. Each TypeScript bridge in `lib/scorer/projection.ts` carries an `ownerSkill`, the skill that owns its command. The generated JSON and generated source blocks are outputs, not hand-edited inputs.\n./.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:86:    expect('COMMAND_POLICIES' in await import('../lib/command-attach.js')).toBe(false);\nexit=0\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"COMMAND_POLICIES\\\" --glob '!specs/**' --glob '!node_modules/**' . | head -20; echo \\\"exit=$?\\\"\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794559548695,"end":1794559549719}}}}
