{"type":"text","timestamp":1794559663639,"sessionID":"ses_e2bee348affe4Stcilr5Lp7I7h","part":{"id":"prt_1d4174d8e002X7Xc0wobm6iQP3","sessionID":"ses_e2bee348affe4Stcilr5Lp7I7h","messageID":"msg_1d4172bd5001nd49o7543Cc4Ei","type":"text","text":"T013 complete. Files changed:\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` — added the async case asserting `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in await import('../lib/command-attach.js')` is `false`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs` — removed `runnablePolicies`, its `set` call, `policyLines`, and the three lines emitting the policy block from `renderCommandRows`.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts` — regenerated by `node $DER`; the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block is gone, `COMMAND_ROWS` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` remain.\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/014-review-remediation/scratch/wg2-slice.txt` — slice test summary lines.\n\nBefore the change, the new case failed as required:\n\n```\nTests  1 failed | 13 passed (14)\nAssertionError: expected true to be false\n```\n\nVerify output after the change:\n\n```\n$ env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  14 passed (14)\n\n$ node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status\nfresh\n\n$ rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" <command-attach.ts> <derive-command-bridges.cjs>\n(no output, exit 1)\n\n$ git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- <command-bridges.generated.json> <projection.ts> <skill_advisor.py>\n(no output, exit 0)\n\n$ cat $SP/wg2-slice.txt\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  4 passed (4)\n```\n\n`node --check $DER` exits 0. One side step: the routing-slice test initially refused to run because the gitignored dist was stale against the edited source, so I ran `npm run build` in the runtime package; the rebuild's attestation is gitignored and no tracked build output changed (confirmed by the empty status above). I did not tick the checkbox. Nothing was left undone.","time":{"start":1794559659406,"end":1794559663639}}}
